        "triangle wave" to """Graphs only. \(y = 2\operatorname{tw}(x)\) zig-zags between \(-2\) and 2.""",
        "logistic sigmoid" to """Graphs only. \(y = \sigma(x - 3)\) is \(\frac{1}{2}\) at 3; \(\sigma'(x) = \sigma(x)(1 - \sigma(x))\).""",
        "softplus" to """Graphs only. Compare \(y = \operatorname{softplus}(x)\) with \(y = \operatorname{ramp}(x)\).""",
        "clamp" to """Graphs only. \(y = \operatorname{clamp}(x, -1, 1)\) is cut off at \(\pm 1\).""",
        "linear interpolation" to """Graphs only. Fill \(a\), \(b\), \(t\): \(\operatorname{lerp}(0, 10, \frac{1}{2}) = 5\).""",
        "smoothstep" to """Graphs only. \(y = S\left(\frac{x}{2}\right)\) eases from 0 to 1 over \([0, 2]\).""",
        "Gaussian" to """Graphs only. \(y = g\left(\frac{x}{2}\right)\) is twice as wide; normpdf is the normalized one.""",
        "wrap" to """Graphs only. \(y = \operatorname{wrap}(x, -1, 1)\) repeats the line between \(-1\) and 1.""",
        // ---- Number pad and symbols
        "all clear" to """Clears the line. Long-press backspace does the same.""",
        "brackets" to """Opens a bracket; the next one closes it. \(2(3 + 4) = 14\).""",
        "divide" to """Makes a fraction: what's before the cursor goes on top. \(\frac{1}{3} + \frac{1}{6} = \frac{1}{2}\).""",
        "times" to """\(6 \cdot 7 = 42\). Next to a letter or bracket you can leave it out: \(2x\).""",
        "minus" to """\(5 - 8 = -3\); also a negative sign.""",
        "plus" to """\(\frac{1}{2} + \frac{1}{3} = \frac{5}{6}\).""",
        "point" to """Decimals: \(0.1 + 0.2 = \frac{3}{10}\), kept exact.""",
        "backspace" to """Deletes before the cursor; a long-press clears everything.""",
        "enter" to """Works the line out. Long-press it for the steps when there are some.""",
        "x" to """The variable: \(x^2 - 1 = 0\) gives \(x = \pm 1\). Other letters are on the Aα tab.""",
        "list of constants with names" to """Opens every constant with its name, value and units; search by name (\(c\), Planck…) and tap one to type it. \(m_e c^2\) gives the electron's rest energy.""",
        "symbol builder" to """Build a symbol like \(\hat{x}_1\): it acts as one letter (one backspace deletes it). Saved symbols appear at the top of this tab.""",
